# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers per path.
#
# Owners are auto-added as required reviewers when a PR touches a path
# they own. The current repo is a single-author project (@sh-ai-x owns
# everything), but the granular rules below let future maintainers scope
# their review responsibility as the team grows.
#
# Format reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default: any change requires an owner review.
*                                          @sh-ai-x

# Hot paths — changes here need extra eyes from the rules-of-the-repo
# author. These match the policy files in rules/ so a rule change has to
# walk past the author before it lands.
/rules/                                    @sh-ai-x
/CLAUDE.md                                 @sh-ai-x

# Security-adjacent — secret-scan, cost-gate, and the auth surface live
# here, plus the run-commands hook scripts that execute arbitrary bash.
# A bypass here is a bypass of the project's enforcement layer; require
# owner review at minimum.
# (combined rule for hooks + .githooks + the security skill)
hooks/*.sh                                 @sh-ai-x
/.githooks/                                @sh-ai-x
skills/security/                           @sh-ai-x
skills/secret-scan/                        @sh-ai-x

# Release / version contract — bump the plugin version + manifest atom.
.claude-plugin/                            @sh-ai-x
.github/workflows/version-bump.yml         @sh-ai-x
.github/workflows/ci.yml                   @sh-ai-x
.github/workflows/review.yml               @sh-ai-x

# Hand-off / dispatch tools — the routing layer between agents and CLI.
tools/parallel_dispatch.py                 @sh-ai-x
tools/token_efficiency_analyzer.py         @sh-ai-x
